Z||000004||ggarsk||11-22-1999||07:56 PM||||Rubber Queen has a cup holder that slips in the window. It fits the groove in the door panel and works real good. It's something until somebody comes up with something better.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||11-22-1999||08:47 PM||||Sometime back there was a post on one of the newsletters about a modified cup holder/tray that sits on top of the arm rest on top of the hump between the seats.  I found a rubbermaid unit like the one the guy modified.<P>It is rectangular, about 6" x 9" and about 2- 1/2" deep.  It is laid out to have two cup holders in the front and a square tray with slots for cassette tapes behind it.  The sides curve down a couple of inches and have cleats to grab the carpet.  It is made to sit on the hump between the seats.<P>What he did was to cut off the curved sides making it a flat bottomed tray.  He cut a piece of plywood the size of the tray.  He then stapled grey vinyl fabric face up to the top of the plywood with flaps overhanging the sides about 4 to 6 inches on each side.  He attached velcro strips to the bottom sides of the flaps and then screwed the board to the bottom of the tray.<P>The tray sits on top of the center arm rest with the flaps hanging down each side of the hump with the velcro strips holding the flaps to the carpet on side of the hump.<P>The pictures looked pretty good.<P>I found a tray like this at a thrift store for 75 cents and plan to make the mods.  If it works I'll try to post a picture.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||11-23-1999||12:11 AM||||carrol, I saw that one......<P>It's been a few years, but that idea used to be available off the shelf. The fabric/soft pastic/whatever flaps where usually small sandbags on the end. They where made like that so they would sit on the trans tunnel in RWD cars. Fiero's "tunnel" is so wide tho that I'm not sure if an off the shelf one would fit even if you could find it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shiner||11-23-1999||01:58 AM||||I don't want to offend anyone here, but... I think drink holders have no place on a sports car.  Do Lambo's have cup holders?  I think not.  Besides, anything not BOLTED down in my car gets thrown all over the place!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||11-23-1999||09:17 AM||||With the seats all the way back, there is enough space between the corner of the seat and the console area to fit a can drink or a medium drink from most drive-thru places.  <P>Lean the seat up one notch and you have a place for a big gulp or bladder buster as I call them.<p>[This message has been edited by DJRice (edited 11-23-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||pollock||11-23-1999||12:09 PM||||Unless you're among the "circumferentially challenged," you can do like me: just tuck the cup between your right hip and the center tunnel.  I've never spilled a drop that way.<P>Of course, i have less room for a cup there than i used to.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000010||deceler8||11-23-1999||12:25 PM||||I made a shift console out of oak to replace my shot original. Since I don't have power windows/locks, the console has an oak filler with a hole for a travel mug where the plastic blocker plate was. I also made another filler with no hole for when I'm not drinking and driving (poor choice of words).<P>If only I could get the Image Poster to work (runtime error). ||||reg||1
